# Realtime Usage Guide

## Intent
Practical guide for adding new realtime events, handlers, and integrating with the database.

## Quick Reference

| Direction | Where to Define | Where to Handle | Protocol |
|-----------|----------------|-----------------|----------|
| Client → Broker | `packages/realtime/src/events/client-events.ts` | `apps/realtime/src/handlers/` | WebSocket |
| Server → Broker | `packages/realtime/src/events/server-events.ts` | `apps/realtime/src/handlers/server/` | TCP |
| Broker → Client | `packages/realtime/src/events/broker-events.ts` | React hooks (`on()`) | WebSocket |

## Step 1: Define Events

### Adding a Client Event (Client → Broker)

```ts
// packages/realtime/src/events/client-events.ts
export const clientEvents = {
  // ... existing events

  "reaction:add": {
    input: z.object({
      messageId: z.string(),
      emoji: z.string(),
    }),
  },
} as const satisfies Record<string, EventDefinition>;
```

### Adding a Server Event (Server → Broker via TCP)

```ts
// packages/realtime/src/events/server-events.ts
export const serverEvents = {
  // ... existing events

  "user:status-change": {
    input: z.object({
      userId: z.string(),
      status: z.enum(["online", "away", "offline"]),
    }),
  },
} as const satisfies Record<string, EventDefinition>;
```

### Adding a Broker Event (Broker → Client)

```ts
// packages/realtime/src/events/broker-events.ts
export const brokerEvents = {
  // ... existing events

  "reaction:added": {
    payload: z.object({
      messageId: z.string(),
      emoji: z.string(),
      user: z.object({ id: z.string(), name: z.string() }),
    }),
  },
} as const satisfies Record<string, PayloadDefinition>;
```

## Step 2: Create Handlers (Broker)

### Client Handler Structure

Create a new file in `apps/realtime/src/handlers/`:

```ts
// apps/realtime/src/handlers/reactions/client/add.ts
import { defineClientHandler } from "@repo/realtime/server";
import { getClientInfo } from "@/lib/helpers";

export const reactionAddHandler = defineClientHandler<{
  messageId: string;
  emoji: string;
}>(async (ctx, data) => {
  // ctx.socket - current client socket
  // ctx.session - authenticated user (or null)
  // ctx.io - Socket.IO server instance

  const user = getClientInfo(ctx);

  // Broadcast to room (excluding sender)
  ctx.socket.to(`message:${data.messageId}`).emit("reaction:added", {
    messageId: data.messageId,
    emoji: data.emoji,
    user,
  });
});
```

### Server Handler Structure

```ts
// apps/realtime/src/handlers/server/server/user-status.ts
import { defineServerHandler } from "@repo/realtime/server";

export const userStatusChangeHandler = defineServerHandler<{
  userId: string;
  status: "online" | "away" | "offline";
}>(async (ctx, data) => {
  // ctx.io - Socket.IO server

  // Emit to specific user's room
  ctx.io.to(`user:${data.userId}`).emit("user:status", { status: data.status });
});
```

### Register Handlers

```ts
// apps/realtime/src/handlers/_app.ts
import { reactionAddHandler } from "./reactions/client/add";
import { userStatusChangeHandler } from "./server/server/user-status";

export const clientHandlers = {
  // ... existing handlers
  "reaction:add": reactionAddHandler,
};

export const serverHandlers = {
  // ... existing handlers
  "user:status-change": userStatusChangeHandler,
};
```

## Step 3: Use in Client (React)

### Setup Provider

```tsx
// apps/web/app/layout.tsx or specific layout
import { RealtimeProvider } from "@repo/realtime/client";
import { getRealtimeUrl } from "@/lib/discovery/realtime";

export default function Layout({ children }) {
  const realtimeUrl = await getRealtimeUrl();

  return (
    <RealtimeProvider url={realtimeUrl}>
      {children}
    </RealtimeProvider>
  );
}
```

### Emit Events from Client

```tsx
import { useSocket } from "@repo/realtime/client";

function MessageReactions({ messageId }: { messageId: string }) {
  const { emit, isConnected } = useSocket();

  const addReaction = (emoji: string) => {
    emit("reaction:add", { messageId, emoji });
  };

  return (
    <button onClick={() => addReaction("👍")} disabled={!isConnected}>
      👍
    </button>
  );
}
```

### Listen to Broker Events

```tsx
import { useSocket } from "@repo/realtime/client";
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

function MessageReactions({ messageId }: { messageId: string }) {
  const { on } = useSocket();
  const [reactions, setReactions] = useState<Reaction[]>([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    const unsubscribe = on("reaction:added", (payload) => {
      if (payload.messageId === messageId) {
        setReactions((prev) => [...prev, payload]);
      }
    });

    return unsubscribe;
  }, [on, messageId]);

  return <div>{/* render reactions */}</div>;
}
```

## Step 4: Emit from Server (oRPC/Next.js)

### Using the Realtime Service

```ts
// packages/server/src/routers/messages/mutations/add-reaction.ts
import { realtime } from "@/services/realtime.service";

export const addReactionHandler = protectedProcedure
  .input(addReactionSchema)
  .handler(async ({ input, context }) => {
    // Save to database
    const reaction = await db.insert(reactions).values({
      messageId: input.messageId,
      userId: context.session.user.id,
      emoji: input.emoji,
    });

    // Notify via realtime (Server → Broker → Clients)
    await realtime.emit("notification:send", {
      userId: messageAuthorId,
      title: "New reaction",
      message: `${context.session.user.name} reacted with ${input.emoji}`,
    });

    return reaction;
  });
```

## Database Integration (Broker-side)

### Creating a Database Service

```ts
// apps/realtime/src/lib/my-feature/database.ts
import { drizzle } from "drizzle-orm/node-postgres";
import { Pool } from "pg";
import { env } from "../env";

const pool = new Pool({ connectionString: env.DATABASE_URL });
export const db = drizzle({ client: pool });
```

### Using Database in Handlers

```ts
// apps/realtime/src/handlers/reactions/client/add.ts
import { defineClientHandler } from "@repo/realtime/server";
import { db } from "@/lib/reactions/database";
import { reactions } from "@repo/database/schema";

export const reactionAddHandler = defineClientHandler<{
  messageId: string;
  emoji: string;
}>(async (ctx, data) => {
  if (!ctx.session) {
    ctx.socket.emit("error", { message: "Authentication required" });
    return;
  }

  // Save to database directly from broker
  await db.insert(reactions).values({
    messageId: data.messageId,
    userId: ctx.session.user.id,
    emoji: data.emoji,
  });

  // Then broadcast
  ctx.socket.to(`message:${data.messageId}`).emit("reaction:added", {
    messageId: data.messageId,
    emoji: data.emoji,
    user: { id: ctx.session.user.id, name: ctx.session.user.name },
  });
});
```

### Debounced Persistence (like Yjs documents)

For high-frequency updates, use debounced saves:

```ts
// apps/realtime/src/lib/feature/operations.ts
const SAVE_DEBOUNCE_MS = 3000;
const pendingSaves = new Map<string, NodeJS.Timeout>();

export function scheduleSave(id: string, saveFn: () => Promise<void>) {
  const existing = pendingSaves.get(id);
  if (existing) clearTimeout(existing);

  pendingSaves.set(
    id,
    setTimeout(async () => {
      await saveFn();
      pendingSaves.delete(id);
    }, SAVE_DEBOUNCE_MS),
  );
}
```

## Handler Context Reference

### Client Handler Context

```ts
interface ClientHandlerContext {
  socket: Socket;              // Current client socket
  session: AuthSession | null; // User session (null if anonymous)
  io: Server;                  // Socket.IO server instance
}
```

### Server Handler Context

```ts
interface ServerHandlerContext {
  io: Server;               // Socket.IO server instance
}
```

## Common Patterns

### Broadcast to Room

```ts
// To all in room except sender
ctx.socket.to(roomId).emit("event", payload);

// To all in room including sender
ctx.io.to(roomId).emit("event", payload);
```

### Send to Specific User

```ts
// Users auto-join their user room on connect
ctx.io.to(`user:${userId}`).emit("event", payload);
```

## Folder Structure Convention

```
apps/realtime/src/handlers/
├── _app.ts                    # Aggregates all handlers
├── rooms/                     # Feature: chat rooms
│   ├── client/                # Client → Broker handlers
│   │   ├── index.ts
│   │   ├── join.ts
│   │   └── message-send.ts
│   ├── utils/                 # Feature-specific utilities
│   │   └── state.ts
│   └── index.ts
├── documents/                 # Feature: collaborative docs
│   ├── client/
│   └── index.ts
└── server/                    # Server → Broker handlers
    └── server/
        ├── index.ts
        └── notification-send.ts
```

## Checklist for New Events

1. [ ] Define event schema in `packages/realtime/src/events/`
2. [ ] Create handler in `apps/realtime/src/handlers/`
3. [ ] Register handler in `apps/realtime/src/handlers/_app.ts`
4. [ ] Use in client with `emit()` or `on()`
5. [ ] (Optional) Use `realtime.emit()` from server
6. [ ] Run `pnpm checks` to validate types
